# FLRW cosmology, the geometry of the expanding universe, modeled by the kernel. The Friedmann-Lemaitre-Robertson-Walker
# universe is homogeneous (the same everywhere) and isotropic (the same in every direction), and it carries one degree of
# freedom that changes with cosmic time: the SCALE FACTOR a(t). Every comoving separation between galaxies is multiplied
# by a(t) to give the physical distance, so as a(t) grows the whole universe stretches and galaxies recede from one
# another. The big bang is the start of cosmic time, the epoch zero, and there is nothing before it: the scale factor is
# minimal there and only ever increases. That one-way growth is the arrow of cosmic time, the same one-way growth the
# wake gives the mesh.
#
# This file MODELS the discrete expansion. The continuous Friedmann equations are not kernel-expressible, so cosmic time
# is a Peano natural (the epoch, the big bang at zero, each tick later) and the scale factor is a natural that grows each
# tick. We commit to a(t) = t + 1 (the scale factor is the successor of the epoch), the simplest law that starts above
# zero and strictly increases. From it we PROVE, by the kernel computing normal forms (`calm hold`) and by structural
# induction (`fold`):
#   the universe EXPANDS: a(t+1) is strictly above a(t), for every epoch (one-way growth, the arrow of cosmic time),
#   the big bang is the MINIMUM: a(0) is at most a(t), for every epoch (nothing precedes the big bang),
#   HUBBLE'S LAW (monotone form): at a fixed epoch a galaxy with a larger comoving separation lies at a larger physical
#     distance, the farther galaxy recedes faster,
#   COSMOLOGICAL REDSHIFT: light emitted at an earlier epoch and observed at a later one is stretched, the redshift
#     factor is at least one (the wavelength grows with the universe),
#   the expansion COMPOUNDS: for a fixed comoving separation the physical distance at a later epoch is at least the
#     physical distance at an earlier one (galaxies recede as space itself grows).

# A natural number: zero, or the successor of a natural. Reused as both the epoch (cosmic time) and the magnitudes of
# the scale factor and distances.
form natural
  case zero
  case succ
    link prior, like natural

# A truth bit, the result of the order comparison. on means the comparison holds.
form bit
  case off
  case on

# Addition by recursion on the first argument: 0 + b = b, (succ a) + b = succ (a + b). Verified terminating and unfolded
# by the kernel.
task plus
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      send back
        read b
    case succ
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            call plus
              read prior
              read b

# Multiplication by recursion on the first argument: 0 * b = 0, (succ a) * b = b + (a * b). This is how a comoving
# separation is scaled into a physical distance.
task times
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      send back
        make zero
    case succ
      send back
        call plus
          read b
          call times
            read prior
            read b

# at-most a b = on iff a <= b. Recurses on both arguments at once (the field-rename binding names each predecessor),
# the decidable order on the naturals. This is the relation behind "the scale factor never shrinks" and "the redshift
# factor is at least one".
task at-most
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like bit
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      send back
        make on
    case succ
      link ap
      fork case, read b
        case zero
          send back
            make off
        case succ
          link bp
          send back
            call at-most
              read ap
              read bp

# --- The cosmology layer. ---

# The epoch: cosmic time as a Peano natural. The big bang is zero, and each tick is one later. Time only moves forward,
# so the epoch only ever counts up.
form epoch
  case bang
  case tick
    link prior, like epoch

# The cosmic time of an epoch as a plain natural: the big bang is zero ticks, each tick adds one. This bridges the epoch
# to the arithmetic, so the scale factor can be computed from it.
task cosmic-time
  take e, like epoch
  like natural
  fork case, read e
    case bang
      send back
        make zero
    case tick
      link prior
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            call cosmic-time
              read prior

# The scale factor a(t), a monotonically increasing function of the epoch. We commit to a(t) = t + 1: the successor of
# the cosmic time. It starts at one at the big bang (never zero) and grows by one each tick, so the universe only ever
# expands.
task scale-factor
  take e, like epoch
  like natural
  send back
    make succ
      bind prior
        call cosmic-time
          read e

# The physical distance between two galaxies: the scale factor at an epoch times their fixed comoving separation. As the
# scale factor grows the same comoving separation maps to an ever larger physical distance, which is the stretching of
# space itself.
task physical-distance
  take e, like epoch
  take comoving, like natural
  like natural
  send back
    call times
      call scale-factor
        read e
      read comoving

# The stretch, the physical distance written with the comoving separation as the left factor and the scale factor on
# the right: separation times scale factor. Equal in value to the physical distance, but in this order the growing scale
# factor is the right argument, which is the shape the compounding law multiplies through.
task stretch
  take comoving, like natural
  take e, like epoch
  like natural
  send back
    call times
      read comoving
      call scale-factor
        read e

# The redshift comparison: light emitted at one epoch and observed at another is stretched by the ratio of the scale
# factors a(observe) / a(emit). We model the stretch as the order fact a(emit) <= a(observe): the redshift factor is at
# least one exactly when the scale factor at observation is at least the scale factor at emission. on means redshifted.
task redshift-at-least-one
  take emit, like epoch
  take observe, like epoch
  like bit
  send back
    call at-most
      call scale-factor
        read emit
      call scale-factor
        read observe

# --- Step lemmas, definitional and inductive, stated so the cosmological laws below can rewrite the recurrences and the
# arithmetic into view. These are the arithmetic of the naturals, included so the file is self-contained. ---

# 0 <= n, always. Definitional.
rule at-most-zero-left-is-on
  seat n, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        make zero
        read n
      make on
  calm hold

# (succ a) <= (succ b) iff a <= b. Definitional.
rule at-most-succ-both
  seat a, like natural
  seat b, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        make succ
          bind prior
            read a
        make succ
          bind prior
            read b
      call at-most
        read a
        read b
  calm hold

# n <= n, always (reflexivity of the order). By induction on n.
rule at-most-reflexive
  seat n, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        read n
        read n
      make on
  fold n

# (succ a) + b = succ (a + b). Definitional, the recurrence of plus.
rule plus-succ-left-steps
  seat a, like natural
  seat b, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call plus
        make succ
          bind prior
            read a
        read b
      make succ
        bind prior
          call plus
            read a
            read b
  calm hold

# n + 0 = n (zero is a right identity). By induction on n.
rule plus-zero-right-is-identity
  seat n, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call plus
        read n
        make zero
      read n
  fold n

# a + (succ b) = succ (a + b) (the successor steps out on the right). By induction on a.
rule plus-succ-right-steps-out
  seat a, like natural
  seat b, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call plus
        read a
        make succ
          bind prior
            read b
      make succ
        bind prior
          call plus
            read a
            read b
  fold a

# Addition is associative: (a + b) + c = a + (b + c). By induction on a.
rule plus-is-associative
  seat a, like natural
  seat b, like natural
  seat c, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call plus
        call plus
          read a
          read b
        read c
      call plus
        read a
        call plus
          read b
          read c
  fold a

# Addition is commutative: a + b = b + a. By induction on a, chaining the right identity and right step lemmas.
rule plus-is-commutative
  seat a, like natural
  seat b, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call plus
        read a
        read b
      call plus
        read b
        read a
  fold a
    cite plus-zero-right-is-identity
    cite plus-succ-right-steps-out

# (succ a) * b = b + (a * b). Definitional, the recurrence of times.
rule times-succ-left-steps-out
  seat a, like natural
  seat b, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call times
        make succ
          bind prior
            read a
        read b
      call plus
        read b
        call times
          read a
          read b
  calm hold

# a * (succ b) = a + (a * b) (the successor steps out on the right of a product). By induction on a, normalizing the
# additive chain modulo associativity and commutativity.
rule times-succ-right-is-plus
  seat a, like natural
  seat b, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call times
        read a
        make succ
          bind prior
            read b
      call plus
        read a
        call times
          read a
          read b
  fold a
    cite times-succ-left-steps-out
    cite plus-succ-left-steps
    cite plus-is-associative
    cite plus-is-commutative

# Left distributivity: a * (b + c) = a*b + a*c. By induction on a, normalizing modulo associativity and commutativity.
rule times-distributes-left
  seat a, like natural
  seat b, like natural
  seat c, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call times
        read a
        call plus
          read b
          read c
      call plus
        call times
          read a
          read b
        call times
          read a
          read c
  fold a
    cite times-succ-left-steps-out
    cite plus-is-commutative
    cite plus-is-associative

# Anything is at most itself plus more: at-most a (a + c) = on, for every a and c. By induction on a. This is the order
# fact that adding a nonnegative amount never decreases a value, the engine behind Hubble's law and the compounding.
rule at-most-self-plus
  seat a, like natural
  seat c, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        read a
        call plus
          read a
          read c
      make on
  fold a
    cite plus-succ-left-steps
    cite at-most-succ-both

# Anything is at most more plus itself: at-most a (c + a) = on. The commuted form, peeling the right summand.
rule at-most-plus-self
  seat a, like natural
  seat c, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        read a
        call plus
          read c
          read a
      make on
  fold a
    cite plus-succ-left-steps
    cite plus-succ-right-steps-out
    cite at-most-succ-both
    cite plus-zero-right-is-identity

# Scaling preserves the order when a gap is added to the right factor: at-most (k*a) (k*(a + c)) = on. By induction on
# k, distributing k over the sum and then applying self-plus. This is the monotonicity that becomes Hubble's law.
rule at-most-times-self-plus
  seat k, like natural
  seat a, like natural
  seat c, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        call times
          read k
          read a
        call times
          read k
          call plus
            read a
            read c
      make on
  fold k
    cite times-distributes-left
    cite at-most-self-plus

# Bumping the right factor by one preserves the order: at-most (k*m) (k*(succ m)) = on. By induction on m, stepping the
# product out on the right and applying plus-self. This is the monotonicity that becomes the compounding of expansion.
rule at-most-times-succ-right
  seat k, like natural
  seat m, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        call times
          read k
          read m
        call times
          read k
          make succ
            bind prior
              read m
      make on
  fold m
    cite times-succ-right-is-plus
    cite at-most-plus-self

# The scale factor at the next tick is the successor of the scale factor now: a(tick e) = succ (a e). Definitional, the
# one-step recurrence of the expansion. The kernel unfolds cosmic-time and scale-factor to see it.
rule scale-factor-tick-is-succ
  seat e, like epoch
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call scale-factor
        make tick
          bind prior
            read e
      make succ
        bind prior
          call scale-factor
            read e
  calm hold

# --- The cosmological laws. ---

# THE UNIVERSE EXPANDS: the scale factor now is at most the scale factor at the next tick, a(e) <= a(tick e), for every
# epoch. The universe never shrinks. With the strict law below this is one-way growth, the arrow of cosmic time.
rule scale-factor-grows-each-tick
  seat e, like epoch
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        call scale-factor
          read e
        call scale-factor
          make tick
            bind prior
              read e
      make on
  fold e
    cite scale-factor-tick-is-succ
    cite at-most-succ-both
    cite at-most-reflexive

# STRICT one-way growth: the scale factor at the next tick is NOT at most the scale factor now, a(tick e) <= a(e) is off.
# Together with the law above this is strict expansion: a(e) < a(tick e), never equal, never reversed. The universe never
# shrinks back and never holds still.
rule scale-factor-strictly-grows
  seat e, like epoch
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        call scale-factor
          make tick
            bind prior
              read e
        call scale-factor
          read e
      make off
  fold e
    cite scale-factor-tick-is-succ
    cite at-most-succ-both
    cite at-most-reflexive

# THE BIG BANG IS THE MINIMUM: the scale factor at the big bang is at most the scale factor at any epoch, a(bang) <= a(e),
# for every epoch. Nothing precedes the big bang. Its scale factor (one) is the smallest the universe ever has.
rule big-bang-is-the-minimum
  seat e, like epoch
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        call scale-factor
          make bang
        call scale-factor
          read e
      make on
  fold e
    cite at-most-succ-both
    cite at-most-zero-left-is-on

# HUBBLE'S LAW (monotone form): at any fixed scale factor (the value the scale factor takes at an epoch), a galaxy whose
# comoving separation is larger by a gap lies at a larger physical distance, scale * near <= scale * (near + gap). The
# recession scales with distance: the farther galaxy is carried away faster as the scale factor multiplies its larger
# separation. The physical distance is scale times separation, so this is the monotonicity of that product in the
# separation, holding for the scale factor at every epoch (the scale factor is one such value). By induction on the
# scale factor, distributing it over the sum and applying self-plus.
rule hubble-law-farther-is-farther
  seat scale, like natural
  seat near, like natural
  seat gap, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        call times
          read scale
          read near
        call times
          read scale
          call plus
            read near
            read gap
      make on
  fold scale
    cite times-distributes-left
    cite at-most-self-plus

# COSMOLOGICAL REDSHIFT: light emitted at the big bang and observed at any epoch is redshifted, the stretch factor is at
# least one. redshift-at-least-one bang e = on, for every epoch. The earliest light is stretched the most as the universe
# expands from its minimum scale factor.
rule redshift-from-the-big-bang
  seat e, like epoch
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call redshift-at-least-one
        make bang
        read e
      make on
  fold e
    cite at-most-succ-both
    cite at-most-zero-left-is-on

# REDSHIFT ALONG A FORWARD STEP: light emitted at an epoch and observed one tick later is redshifted, redshift e (tick e)
# = on, for every epoch. Each tick of cosmic time stretches the wavelength a little more, the redshift factor staying at
# least one because the scale factor only grows.
rule redshift-across-one-tick
  seat e, like epoch
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call redshift-at-least-one
        read e
        make tick
          bind prior
            read e
      make on
  fold e
    cite scale-factor-tick-is-succ
    cite at-most-succ-both
    cite at-most-reflexive

# THE EXPANSION COMPOUNDS: for a fixed comoving separation, the physical distance grows when the scale factor steps up by
# one, d * scale <= d * (succ scale). Since the scale factor steps up by exactly one each tick (scale-factor-tick-is-succ
# above), this is the physical distance at an epoch being at most the physical distance one tick later: galaxies recede
# as space itself grows, the same comoving separation mapping to an ever larger physical distance with each tick. By
# induction on the scale factor, stepping the product out on the right and applying plus-self.
rule expansion-compounds
  seat d, like natural
  seat scale, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-most
        call times
          read d
          read scale
        call times
          read d
          make succ
            bind prior
              read scale
      make on
  fold scale
    cite times-succ-right-is-plus
    cite at-most-plus-self
